WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:05.620
Just two episodes after Game of Thrones gave
Arya Stark a stunning romance scene, the series

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.799
completely dropped the ball with another female
character at least in the eyes of countless

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:10.780
fans around the world.

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:12.840
Beware... spoilers are coming!

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.100
The fourth episode of Game of Thrones' final
season, "The Last of the Starks," picked up

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.040
right after the brutal Battle of Winterfell.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:24.840
Before Arya Stark vanquished the Night King
and his frosty minions, many good people sacrificed

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.880
their lives to protect Winterfell and the
rest of Westeros.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.840
Daenerys Targaryen and Jon Snow attempted
to flame out the enemy with their dragons,

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.879
and Brienne of Tarth put her new status as
a Knight of the Seven Kingdoms to use, fighting

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.960
the White Walkers as the commander of her
own section of soldiers.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:43.960
One of those soldiers was the man who knighted
her: Jaime Lannister.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.320
Brienne and Jaime have had a complex history
throughout the run of Game of Thrones.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.180
The pair first met in season 2, when he was
her prisoner.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.680
They eventually grew closer throughout the
course of the series, but they've certainly

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:55.860
had more than a few clashes.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.780
Jaime even gave Brienne his Valyrian steel
sword Oathkeeper for her mission to keep the

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:08.720
Stark girls safe.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:13.280
Clearly, there's a lot of love between Jaime
and Brienne, but nothing ever came of their

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:18.040
feelings… perhaps because Jaime has been
blindly in love with his sister, Cersei.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:23.540
That all changed on season 8, episode 4, when
Jaime and Brienne shared an intimate night

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.240
together after a drinking game took a turn
for the personal.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:29.060
The romantic moment was everything you could've
hoped for.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:32.979
But then, the show took that shiny moment
and tarnished it in a flash.

00:01:32.979 --> 00:01:37.170
In the eyes of many viewers, the romantic
scene was ruined just a few minutes after

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:42.640
it all went down, when word got out that Euron
Greyjoy had ambushed Daenerys' fleet and slaughtered

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.000
her dragon Rhaegal.

00:01:44.329 --> 00:01:49.240
Worse still, news reached Winterfell that
Cersei's minions had captured Daenerys' Handmaiden

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:49.840
Missandei.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:54.040
Shortly after Brienne delivered the terrible
news to Jaime, he slipped away into the night

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.120
to head for King's Landing.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.820
What he plans to do there is a mystery…
but Jaime's departure left Brienne utterly

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:00.820
broken-hearted.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.439
"You're a good man and you can't save her.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.220
You don't need to die with her.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:06.960
Stay here."

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:14.430
As Brienne sobs, Jaime runs through all the
the horrific things he's done over the years

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:18.880
for Cersei, like pushing Bran Stark out of
a window and paralyzing him for life.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.140
Attempting to show Brienne who he truly is,
he says:

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:27.120
"She's hateful, and so am I."

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:35.520
And with that, Jaime rides off to King's Landing
and Brienne's soft sobs echo through the night.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:38.340
Fans immediately took to Twitter to express
their distress:

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:41.620
"Brienne crying is something i never want
to see again."

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.440
Another Twitter user was evidently having
a breakdown:

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:49.290
"... what should have been our Jaime and Brienne
moment got COMPLETELY RUINED AND I'M SO ANGRY

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.460
I WANT TO CRY"

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:54.040
Another fan took aim at the Game of Thrones
writers, tweeting:

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.659
"good morning i only came online to say that
brienne deserves better &amp; the writers completely

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.760
ruined YEARS of jaime's development…"

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.980
One viewer defended the scene, writing:

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:07.400
"[Brienne is] crying because she, more than
anyone, has seen his character growth and

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.400
now he's turning his back on that growth.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:10.480
He's giving up."

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:14.180
Clearly, the Jaime and Brienne romance has
ruffled a lot of feathers.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:19.360
But there's a potential bright side: Jaime
might be going to King's Landing to kill Cersei.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:23.360
Perhaps he's planning to return to Winterfell
to live out the rest of his days with Brienne.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:28.380
Could the Kingslayer possibly become the Queenslayer,
and then become Brienne's new beau on the

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:29.980
next episode of Game of Thrones?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.740
We'll simply have to wait and see.

